            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Large",
            "weight": "Bolder",
            "text": "The full Ninth Circuit, 6–5, upheld Hawaii’s 30-day purchase-permit limit and its pre-possession police inspection.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "text": "In Yukutake v. Lopez, the en banc court read Bruen’s footnote nine as making objective, non-abusive shall-issue permit systems presumptively constitutional, reversing a 2025 panel. The ruling binds federal courts in nine western states, including Washington and California, and changes no law.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
